{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2796","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2796","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2796\",\"parent_revision\":\"fcea4a7af89bfaacd5c935046898126dd310d58ce089252acd6bb24440cbc721\",\"root_revision\":\"fcea4a7af89bfaacd5c935046898126dd310d58ce089252acd6bb24440cbc721\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P2\\ntype: Refactor\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nA verified mapping of all 47 distinct MCP tools referenced across plugins/development-harness/*.md (excluding agents/*.md) against the actual CLI command surface (plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/cli.py's 5 command groups: plan, backlog, dispatch, artifact, active-task) found 10 tools/parameters with no full CLI equivalent, out of scope for a mechanical doc-rewrite pass:\\n\\nNo CLI equivalent at all (7): dispatch_conflicts, dispatch_stale_check, profile_list, profile_load, sync_now, sync_status, and sam_state (this last one may not even be a currently-registered MCP tool at all -- it does not appear in this session's dh:sam MCP tool listing alongside sam_task/sam_plan/sam_active_task, and needs an existence-check before any doc assumes it maps to anything).\\n\\nPartial CLI equivalent (3): backlog_list's full-text search parameter has no matching --search flag on the CLI's backlog list command (sam_plan's plan list command does have --search, so the gap is specific to backlog list, not systemic); sam_plan's create action accepts multiple tasks in one call while the CLI's plan create accepts only one inline task per invocation (plan append-task covers additional tasks but changes the call shape); backlog_view/backlog_update have MCP-only capabilities (progressive-disclosure ordinal navigation for view; verified-label and struck-entry operations for update) with no CLI-side equivalent.\\n\\nImpact: any documentation or workflow that needs one of these 10 capabilities cannot fully migrate off MCP onto the CLI as currently built. This blocks a complete CLI migration for the small number of files/workflows that use these specific capabilities, even though the majority (~40 of 47) of MCP tool calls do have full CLI parity and are being converted separately.\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **maintainer of the codebase**, I want to **10 mcp tools/params used in development-harness docs have no or partial cli equivalent** so that **the code is cleaner and more maintainable**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation 2026-08-05, following mapping work for PR #2781 (feat(sam): integrate modular CLI command groups)\\n- **Priority**: P2\\n- **Added**: 2026-08-05\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-08-05)\\n\\n### Additional Gaps Found During Write-Phase\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-05T06:15:32.057265Z</sub>\\n\\nDiscovered by workers while actually converting the 48 files (not caught by the tool-level mapping pass, since these are per-parameter gaps on otherwise-\\\"Full\\\" tools):\\n\\n1. `backlog_groom(..., append=True)` \u2014 CLI's `backlog groom` has no `--append` flag. Two call sites in implement-feature/SKILL.md left as MCP rather than guess default write semantics.\\n2. `artifact_register(...)` calls that don't supply an `artifact_id` value \u2014 CLI's `artifact register` lists `--artifact-id` as required, and it's unconfirmed whether it can be derived/defaulted from `--artifact-type`. Two T0/TN bookend-registration call sites in implement-feature/SKILL.md left as MCP.\\n3. `backlog_add(..., plan=...)` in interop/SKILL.md \u2014 CLI's `backlog add` has no `--plan` flag. Worth checking whether `plan` was ever a real parameter on the MCP `backlog_add` tool itself before treating this as a CLI-specific gap \u2014 the MCP tool's own schema (title/priority/description/source/type/force) doesn't list a `plan` param either, so this may be a pre-existing doc inaccuracy on both sides, not a CLI-only gap.\\n\\nSeparately, a distinct architectural finding (not a tool/parameter gap): the workflow-graph extraction pipeline (graph-schema.md's assembler rule, prd-workflow-extractor.md's extraction rules) only recognizes MCP-form call syntax (`mcp__plugin_dh_*__tool(...)` and short `tool(...)` forms) when building mcp_tool nodes. Files now using CLI-form calls (`uv run .../cli.py <command>`) are invisible to that extraction, so the workflow graph will under-count tool-call edges for every file converted in this session's rewrite pass. Flagged in the extraction-rule docs themselves but the actual extraction script was not touched (separate implementation task, not a doc-only fix).\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"51fb3bd80250807cbd32c28051e8083ed856e8e6f7cf60d256c649e9a55a9947\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPg7MoQ\"}"}